   "explain_l1": "A counter is the small noun that follows a number: 人 for people, 本 for long thin things, 枚 for flat ones, 台 for machines and vehicles, 回 for occurrences, 試合 for matches. The sound shifts look random but are not: 一本 is いっぽん, 三本 is さんぼん, 六本 is ろっぽん, and 人 runs ひとり, ふたり, さんにん, よにん, while 何人 is なんにん. 回 and 試合 are the pair you need to schedule a season; 人 is the one you need inside a club. つ covers only one to ten, and only things that have no counter of their own.",
